outline.doc:
Load data from some place and normalize it into a Corpus.

Subclasses own the details of where data lives and how it is shaped;
the rest of the pipeline only ever sees `Corpus`.

One step of how a system reached its answer, kept for analysis.

`kind` is one of:

- `instructions`: the system instructions the model was given, in `text`;
- `input`: a message the model was given, in `text`;
- `model`: a model turn: its visible `text`, its `thoughts` summary, the `tool_calls`
  it made (each with `tool` and `arguments`) and its token counts;
- `tool`: one tool call: `tool`, `arguments`, the `output` the model received and the
  `doc_ids` of the documents in it.

A person's memory of the document they are asking about: big picture, few details.

Some notes hold one detail that is slightly wrong, as human memory often is;
`wrong_detail` says which, so those questions can be scored apart.

